  "warnings": [
    "lineage agent notes: 1) Possible legacy bug (row fan-out): #money LEFT JOINs both claim_payments and #reserve on claim_id before GROUP BY (lines 109-115). A claim can have up to two reserve rows (INDEMNITY and EXPENSE), so SUM(p.amount) counts each payment once per reserve row, and total_paid and incurred can come out doubled. The migration must reproduce this behaviour to match the legacy output; n_payments is not affected because it uses COUNT(DISTINCT). 2) claim_ref is NULL whenever handler_code is NULL, because string concatenation with + returns NULL by default (CONCAT_NULL_YIELDS_NULL). 3) policy_number comes from the single latest snapshot_date on or before @AsOfDate across the whole table, picked into the variable @snapshot_date (lines 121-123). If a policy is missing from that snapshot, policy_number is NULL; the job does not fall back to an earlier snapshot. 4) Reserve types other than INDEMNITY or EXPENSE are dropped, and the reserve_date filter only changes the reserve values, not which claim rows appear. 5) The PARTITION BY claim_id, reserve_type in the reserve ROW_NUMBER is listed as a ranks edge with lower confidence (0.6). 6) The joins to #money and #reserve keep every open claim, so the output has one row per claim from stg.claims that passes the filters on lines 73-74."
  ]
